<title>JAPAN: Japan March gold imports up 9.2 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan March gold imports up 9.2 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gold imports in March</p>
<p>rose by 9.2 percent from a year earlier to 15.37 tonnes,</p>
<p>Ministry of Finance (MOF) data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>The figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			  Mar 97    Feb 97   Mar 96</p>
<p> Total		  15.37	14.49    14.08</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> South Africa	  2.62	 5.88     2.63</p>
<p> Switzerland	   2.49	 3.54     1.58</p>
<p> Australia	     5.80	 2.23     4.58</p>
<p> Britain		 2.00	 0.50     1.00</p>
<p> South Korea	   0.80	 1.30     0.60</p>
<p>Cumulative gold imports in the first three months of 1997</p>
<p>totalled 41.36 tonnes, down from 44.87 tonnes in the same</p>
<p>period a year earlier year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 7431</p>
</text>
